{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c5aa4712-d95d-47ea-b3ef-c191d7d52fbb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"## Updated Caching Strategy\n\nThe **`build_system`** function in **`bot.py`** now splits the system prompt into two separate **cache‑controlled blocks**:\n\n1. **Static Instructions Block** – never changes, cached with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`.  \n2. **Volatile Athlete Context Block** – contains per‑user data (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language) and also uses an `ephemeral` marker, but is a separate list entry.\n\nThis ensures a `save_fact` write only invalidates the tail block, keeping the static instructions hot in the cache and avoiding full‑prompt token costs on subsequent calls.\n\n### Details of the Change\n- Replaced the single‑block implementation with a two‑block version.\n- Added a clear docstring explaining the rationale.\n- Updated comments to describe each block’s purpose.\n\nThe full change log is documented in **`ANSWER.md`** in the artifact directory.\n","duration_seconds":70.443893,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":34904,"output_tokens":4364,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":314816,"total_tokens":39268}}}
